// [v3.31.14 LOCAL — FIREBASE WORKER SETTLE AFTER TIMEOUT] 2026-09-28
// Problem: v3.31.13 made Firebase AsyncResult storage persistent and deferred socket stop,
// but after a caller timeout fbLoopWork could still run for a few seconds. A later operation
// inside the same RTDB batch then saw workerBusy, producing R372/R373/R377 failures and
// leaving postRoundHealth=worker BUSY.
// Fix: after the bounded caller timeout, fbCzekajImpl marks the operation abandoned but
// waits a second bounded settle window for fbLoopWork to finish safely before returning.
// If the worker finishes during settle, its final AsyncResult is visible to the caller.
// If settle also expires, the function returns with an explicit diagnostic; no unsafe
// concurrent socket stop is introduced. Test-only; production remains v3.19.2.

// [v3.31.13 LOCAL — STABILITY RETRY / FIREBASE RESULT LIFETIME FIX] 2026-09-28
// Problem 1: AsyncResult przekazywany do detached fbLoopWorker mogl byc lokalny
//   i znikac po timeoutcie; worker nadal mial do niego wskaznik.
// Problem 2: po timeoutcie caller mogl wykonac fbSSLClient.stop() rownolegle z
//   fbApp.loop() w workerze.
// Problem 3: R278 porownywal globalne liczniki telemetryki bez synchronizacji;
//   zwykla probka telemetryczna mogla legalnie zmienic counter w trakcie testu.
// Fix: testowe AsyncResult sa trwale (static/global), stop() po timeoutcie jest
//   odraczane do workerowego konca, a liczniki telemetryki maja wspolny mutex,
//   ktory R278 obejmuje na czas adaptera.
